<title>UK: U.S./Bund spread stable, gilt gap widens.</title>
<headline>U.S./Bund spread stable, gilt gap widens.</headline>
<text>
<p>1708 GMT - U.S./Bund spread steady on day's session, wider from Thursday in thin U.S. bond trade. Gilt/Bund spread gaps open as profit-taking erodes part of gilt market's recent gains. BTP/Bund spread stable after Eurostat approves Italy's Euro tax and state railway financing plans for use in reducing the 1997 budget deficit.</p>
<p>10-YEARS	     LAST    PRIOR CLOSE</p>
<p>US/GERMANY	    94	   91</p>
<p>FRANCE/GERMANY     -13	  -14</p>
<p>UK/GERMANY	   172	  170</p>
<p>ITALY/GERMANY	168	  170</p>
<p>Government bond spreads are calculated from Reuter benchmark bond price data and adjusted to take into account interest payment frequency.</p>
